# Use the image CMD instead of replacing it with `sleep infinity`.
#
# The Dockerfile CMD starts httpd (`httpd -k start`) in the background and then
# execs `sleep infinity`, so httpd is ALREADY RUNNING with the vulnerable config
# when the agent starts (making the "fixed config but never restarted" case
# detectable) and PID 1 is the sleep (restarting httpd cannot kill the
# container). A fix MUST restart httpd.
